Hi all,

After some time of lurking, I think it is time for me to add something 
to this newsgroup, and share my my most recent misfortune with you all.

Having ascended a Valk and a Barb, I've been trying some less 
combat-oriented characters. Some monks and wizards were killed, and then 
I got lucky with this tourist.

Henk the neutral tourist started off somewhat oddly, immediately using 
his scrolls of magic mapping to map out the first four levels. This 
proved to be a good choice, however, leaving him with both gauntlets of 
power and a helmet of brilliance. An early sacrifice also yielded 
Mjollnir. Henk proceeded to sokoban and got the bag of holding without 
much trouble.

In the Gnomish mines he was chased by a leocrotta who caught him with 
too little HPs. While Henk was fleeing a nymph joined the hunt. Henk 
discovered a polytrap, and a few moves later the nymph had become a 
storm giant. Henk fled into a narrow passage where the leocrotta was 
disposed of, leaving Henk with only several HPs. The storm giant was 
still approaching though, so Henk decided to pull his blessed scroll of 
taming out of his bag. The giant was tamed, Henk used the polytrap to 
turn his cat into a leocrotta, the mines were finished, and life was good.

Several levels below the oracle Henk found a double bones file in the 
bigroom. A previous character of my own, and some other poor hearse user 
had been unable to survive the horde that had assembled around the 
stairs. Henk managed to cut through, though. The reward was big. GDSM, 
Magicbane, speed boots, two magic lamps and Lots of Stuff. And then Henk 
had not even opened two of the bags of holding yet because they seemed 
to be cursed. Life was getting better and better.

Moving deeper and deeper into the Dungeons of Doom Henk stumbled upon 
the Quest. A wraith corpse on the home level brought him to xlvl 14, so 
Twoflower thought him worthy. The next two levels were explored, but 
Henk decided to turn back then, both because he was collecting so much 
loot that it became very difficult to move around unburdened and because 
he was uncertain if would be ready to face his nemesis. So Henk went 
back to the nearest known altar, which was at dlvl 1, to do some 
BUC-IDing, IDing and enchanting.

On returning to the quest portal, Henk decided it better to move on 
downwards. Down he went, past the rogue level, and then on dlvl 19 he 
found a swampish level. The eels and other water-fauna were easily dealt 
with using just melee attacks. (Never had any drowning problems before, 
doing that.) Henk carefully stepped around the pools, and then some 
couatls came through the hallway. Thinking these would make some nice 
pets, he pulled a blessed scroll of taming out of his bag. He backed up 
into a room trying to get both couatls next to him. This succeeded, but 
one of the couatls was over water. I should also mention now that Henk 
was burdened. (I've never liked making stashes.) Well, Henk even got the 
chance to read the scroll, but only one was tamed. The other pulled him 
under mercilessly.

At the moment I wasn't realizing that couatls can do that (although some 
earlier grabbing could have been a clue), but the most stupid was 
failing to wear my amulet of magical breathing. (It was my only amulet 
after discarding some amulets versus poison.)

Well, with 281389 points I at least broke my own high score on this 
installation.

